"\<11. ATP, ADP and Pi explicit; Gamma of every loop; deficiency (Supplementary Note 3; Supplementary Figs 9B, 11; Supplementary Table 8)\>",
"Section",ExpressionUUID -> "ef2a84fc-9441-47fa-a616-580ee9c05d2e"],Cell[
"\<Add three species, ATP (24), ADP (25) and Pi (26): ATP consumed and ADP released in the kinase catalytic steps R2, R4, R10, R12; Pi released in the phosphatase catalytic steps R6, R8, R14, R16. The rank rises to 18 and four loops remain; none hydrolyses net ATP.\>",
"Text",FontColor -> RGBColor[0,0,1],ExpressionUUID -> "b26794d0-c326-4858-9d61-ad785a6aaa5c"],Cell[
CellGroupData[
{Cell[
"\<S2 = Map[Join[#, {0, 0, 0}] &, S];
Do[S2[[j, 24]] = -1; S2[[j, 25]] = 1, {j, {2, 4, 10, 12}}];
Do[S2[[j, 26]] = 1, {j, {6, 8, 14, 16}}];
rrF = RowReduce[Join[S2, IdentityMatrix[22], 2]];
loopsF = Select[rrF, AllTrue[#[[1 ;; 26]], # == 0 &] &][[All, 27 ;;]];
loopsF = Map[If[First[Select[#, # != 0 &]] < 0, -#, #] &, loopsF];
{MatrixRank[S2], loopText /@ loopsF}\>",
"Input",CellLabel -> "In[65]:= ",ExpressionUUID -> "384da63a-1e84-4664-9772-ad7a744f29fd"],Cell[
BoxData[
RowBox[{"{",RowBox[{"18",",",RowBox[{"{",RowBox[{"\"+R1 +R2 +R7 +R8 -R11 -R12 -R13 -R14\"",",","\"+R3 +R4 +R5 +R6 -R11 -R12 -R13 -R14\"",",","\"+R9 +R10 -R11 -R12 -R13 -R14 +R15 +R16\"",",","\"+R18 +R19 -R20 -R21\""}],"}"}]}],"}"}],
StandardForm],"Output",CellLabel -> "Out[71]= ",ExpressionUUID -> "db45bfe5-1a72-4c7b-b2bd-2f0f698d2052"]},
Open],ExpressionUUID -> "12fbf56c-a64f-4d88-9ef6-52c798c861e4"],Cell[
"\<Gamma of a loop with coefficients nu: lnGamma = Sum nu_j Log[kf_j/kb_j]. With the reference constants, the four PdP cycles carry lnGamma = 19.8 (one ATP per turn) and every ATP-free loop has lnGamma = 0, as thermodynamics requires (Wegscheider condition). That the ATP-free loops F1-F3 combine one PdP cycle forward with cycle 4 backward is why all four cycles must share one value of Gamma.\>",
"Text",FontColor -> RGBColor[0,0,1],ExpressionUUID -> "3eed725a-73b0-4d6c-a77f-5b381bf08e54"],Cell[
CellGroupData[
{Cell[
"\<lnK = Log[kfRef/kbRef];
{Chop[loopsN . lnK, 10^-9], Chop[loopsF . lnK, 10^-9]}\>",
"Input",CellLabel -> "In[72]:= ",ExpressionUUID -> "788df1e2-c098-4ee2-b683-9da77279adf7"],Cell[
BoxData[
RowBox[{"{",RowBox[{RowBox[{"{",RowBox[{"19.8`",",","19.8`",",","19.8`",",","19.800000000000004`",",","0"}],"}"}],",",RowBox[
{"{",RowBox[{"0",",","0",",","0",",","0"}],"}"}]}],"}"}],StandardForm],"Output",CellLabel -> "Out[73]= ",
ExpressionUUID -> "39867341-ed3c-46ad-ab32-238a9c1cf85e"]},Open],ExpressionUUID -> "c2822731-0a21-4571-88ec-08671779c996"],Cell[

"\<Chemical reaction network theory: complexes (the distinct left- and right-hand sides), linkage classes (connected components of the reaction graph) and deficiency = complexes - linkage classes - rank = 5, equal to the number of loops; the number of circuit conditions is p - (n - l) = 0.\>",
"Text",FontColor -> RGBColor[0,0,1],ExpressionUUID -> "876e3583-179a-44a0-90d4-ad1f734c8c05"],Cell[
CellGroupData[
{Cell[
"\<cx = DeleteDuplicates[Flatten[Map[{Sort[#[[1]]], Sort[#[[2]]]} &, rx], 1]];
g = Graph[Range[Length[cx]], Map[UndirectedEdge[Position[cx, Sort[#[[1]]]][[1, 1]],
  Position[cx, Sort[#[[2]]]][[1, 1]]] &, rx]];
{nC, nL} = {Length[cx], Length[ConnectedComponents[g]]};
{nC, nL, MatrixRank[S], nC - nL - MatrixRank[S], 22 - (nC - nL)}\>",
"Input",CellLabel -> "In[74]:= ",ExpressionUUID -> "f9a6efe0-7050-4b55-ab42-50c512a72829"],Cell[
BoxData[
RowBox[{"{",RowBox[{"29",",","7",",","17",",","5",",","0"}],"}"}],StandardForm],"Output",
CellLabel -> "Out[77]= ",ExpressionUUID -> "239b3503-3515-4423-a60f-c7b6f16e2d2b"]},
Open],ExpressionUUID -> "f5ca1276-d29a-43b0-a73c-f734b788f159"],Cell[
"\<12. The split parameter u (Supplementary Note 2, Steps 9-14; Supplementary Table 6; Methods 4.2)\>",
"Section",ExpressionUUID -> "69d28b38-b3a7-4647-8dd7-ddf032b30d00"],Cell[
"\<Step 9. With the ATP drive Gamma and the six given constants fixed, Eq (1) (= Eq S2) contains the two rebinding constants kbb and kbd only through their product rho = kbb kbd (Eq S3). Here it is solved symbolically for kbb: the solution depends on kbd, so thermodynamics fixes only the product.\>",
"Text",FontColor -> RGBColor[0,0,1],ExpressionUUID -> "66951ef6-2518-4869-a446-4948465bce4d"],Cell[
CellGroupData[
{Cell[
"\<eqS2 = gam == kfa kfb kfc kfd/(kba kbb kbc kbd);
Solve[eqS2, kbb]
rhoS3 = kfa kfb kfc kfd/(kba kbc gam)\>",
"Input",CellLabel -> "In[78]:= ",ExpressionUUID -> "41e0e683-ee33-4f4e-ac61-8d808bbf0a4e"],Cell[
BoxData[
RowBox[{"{",RowBox[{"{",RowBox[{"kbb","\[Rule]",FractionBox[RowBox[{"kfa"," ","kfb"," ","kfc"," ","kfd"}],
RowBox[{"gam"," ","kba"," ","kbc"," ","kbd"}]]}],"}"}],"}"}],StandardForm],"Output",
CellLabel -> "Out[79]= ",ExpressionUUID -> "704aaa02-9c65-487c-b2b2-3bed6a6a62dc"],Cell[
BoxData[
FractionBox[RowBox[{"kfa"," ","kfb"," ","kfc"," ","kfd"}],RowBox[{"gam"," ","kba"," ","kbc"}]],
StandardForm],"Output",CellLabel -> "Out[80]= ",ExpressionUUID -> "11ed61d1-00a5-4e8a-a8c8-bb04eface913"]},
Open],ExpressionUUID -> "ee405afb-72ec-4532-87b3-cbcc0f4e5182"],Cell[
"\<Step 10. Definition of u (Eq S4): kbb = Sqrt[rho] 10^u, kbd = Sqrt[rho] 10^-u. The inverse (Eq S5) recovers rho and u from any positive pair, and the ratio kbb/kbd = 10^(2u) depends on u alone (Eq S6). The last line checks the inverse numerically for random rho and u.\>",
"Text",FontColor -> RGBColor[0,0,1],ExpressionUUID -> "cbfe3a14-c170-4df7-8e4d-30d1c7df11f3"],Cell[
CellGroupData[
{Cell[
"\<kbbU = Sqrt[rh] 10^uu; kbdU = Sqrt[rh] 10^-uu;
Simplify[{kbbU kbdU, kbbU/kbdU}, rh > 0]
With[{r0 = RandomReal[{10^-16, 10^-8}], u0 = RandomReal[{-3, 3}]}, {kbbU kbdU/r0,
  Log10[kbbU/kbdU]/2 - u0} /. {rh -> r0, uu -> u0}]\>",
"Input",CellLabel -> "In[81]:= ",ExpressionUUID -> "c4cfaad0-7c88-407b-b473-7b11b223b681"],Cell[
BoxData[
RowBox[{"{",RowBox[{"rh",",",SuperscriptBox["100","uu"]}],"}"}],StandardForm],"Output",
CellLabel -> "Out[82]= ",ExpressionUUID -> "cbe1876f-3b47-478a-b1dc-d84518cc2492"],Cell[
BoxData[
RowBox[{"{",RowBox[{"1.`",",",RowBox[{"-","2.7755575615628914`*^-17"}]}],"}"}],StandardForm],
"Output",CellLabel -> "Out[83]= ",ExpressionUUID -> "9d4a2ead-eaf8-4aab-b763-b810deec214c"]},
Open],ExpressionUUID -> "a7041895-83bf-46fa-bad4-873f6ab5e443"],Cell[
"\<Step 11. Eq (1) holds exactly for every u (Eqs S7, S8): inserting Eq S4 and rho from Eq S3 gives back gam, with no u left.\>",
"Text",FontColor -> RGBColor[0,0,1],ExpressionUUID -> "bac3913c-a41d-4870-b1e0-d6c31ef44a9a"],Cell[
CellGroupData[
{Cell[
"\<Simplify[kfa kfb kfc kfd/(kba kbc kbbU kbdU) /. rh -> rhoS3, {kfa > 0, kfb > 0,
  kfc > 0, kfd > 0, kba > 0, kbc > 0, gam > 0}]\>",
"Input",CellLabel -> "In[84]:= ",ExpressionUUID -> "11526fe5-19f7-4de4-afbe-3026c5cae68b"],Cell[
BoxData[
"gam",StandardForm],"Output",CellLabel -> "Out[84]= ",ExpressionUUID -> "c87bb17e-31a6-4cbb-bcf6-ffb96922ff44"]},
Open],ExpressionUUID -> "14375ad1-717a-4b05-8049-17913f0f671a"],Cell[
"\<Step 12. How u shares the drive between the two half-cycles (Eqs S9-S11). lnKkin = lnKkin0 - u Log[10] and lnKP = lnKP0 + u Log[10]; their sum is lnGamma for every u. Each unit of u moves RT Log[10] = 5.94 kJ/mol between the half-cycles; the +-0.3 of the local ensembles moves 1.78 kJ/mol.\>",
"Text",FontColor -> RGBColor[0,0,1],ExpressionUUID -> "0a03dcc4-b785-4f19-87e1-1ea36c0adc9c"],Cell[
CellGroupData[
{Cell[
"\<lnKkinU = Log[kfa kfb/(kba kbbU)]; lnKPU = Log[kfc kfd/(kbc kbdU)];
Simplify[PowerExpand[{lnKkinU - (Log[kfa kfb/(kba Sqrt[rh])] - uu Log[10]),
  lnKPU - (Log[kfc kfd/(kbc Sqrt[rh])] + uu Log[10])}]]
Simplify[PowerExpand[lnKkinU + lnKPU /. rh -> rhoS3]]
Chop[{lnKkinU - (Log[kfa kfb/(kba Sqrt[rh])] - uu Log[10]),
  lnKPU - (Log[kfc kfd/(kbc Sqrt[rh])] + uu Log[10]),
  (lnKkinU + lnKPU /. rh -> rhoS3) - Log[gam]} /. Thread[{kfa, kfb, kfc, kfd, kba,
  kbc, gam, rh, uu} -> Join[RandomReal[{0.1, 10}, 8], {RandomReal[{-2, 2}]}]],
  10^-9]
{RT Log[10], 0.3 RT Log[10]}\>",
"Input",CellLabel -> "In[85]:= ",ExpressionUUID -> "1161ebb8-144f-4061-950c-adc3c001d9a4"],Cell[
